<p><span lang="EN-GB">Triangles are flat and have two faces, front and back. Sometimes it is impossible to determine the correct facing of a triangle: front or back and the result is distortion in the object view. An object may contain triangles, which are correctly orientated and other triangles, which are not. By applying</span> <span class="Command">Unify Normals</span><span lang="EN-GB">, all the normals in the object are orientated in the same direction as the first triangle in the object. You can view the direction of normals using</span> <span class="Command">Display Normals</span> <span lang="EN-GB">from the</span> <span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>View</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">menu.</span></p>
<p class="Note" id="p1"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Note</b></span>: If after this operation all the normals in the object face the wrong direction, select the whole mesh and call Flip Normals.</p>
<p class="Use"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Use</b></span> <span class="Command">Unify Normals</span> <span lang="EN-GB">for exporting and importing objects, containing triangles with backward normals.</span></p>
